    :overridable-by "KOTOBASE_FOLD_THRESHOLD"
    :how "ctx.waitUntil background fold after a transact whose novelty_size
          crossed the threshold, single-slot claim per graph"
    :its-own-reason "\"the engine's should-fold? default of 64 optimizes write
                     amortization; a read-heavy BaaS pays novelty tax per READ,
                     so we fold far sooner\""}]
  :novelty-size-is-entries-not-hops
  "kotobase-peer's novelty-size reads the O(1) \"novelty-count\" field, i.e. the
   number of unfolded transactions. The sequential round trips are NODES, and
   after c63468f4 a node holds up to novelty-segment-size = 16 entries. So
   novelty_size 63 is NOT 63 hops. push-novelty!'s own docstring: a pre-existing
   single-entry head node is never rewritten -- a new entry starts a fresh segment
   pointing at it -- so a chain written before that landing keeps its old nodes and
   grows segments on top."}

